        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies thoughts of harming others; fears “losing it,” but describes verbal outbursts only."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental status examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, guarded, and engages with encouragement; occasionally tearful when discussing nightmares, with affect more distressed than her words suggest. Appropriate appearance and good hygiene. Tense, fidgety, and scanning the room; reluctant to elaborate unless prompted. Speech normal in rate and volume, becoming louder when describing conflict. Mood described as “pissed off all the time”; affect irritable, mildly anxious, congruent, and reactive. Thought form linear and goal-directed. Intrusive trauma memories; no delusions. No hallucinations. Cognition grossly intact, with some difficulty maintaining focus on longer questions. Partial insight; judgement intact regarding safety."
      }
